    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6832" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακτόριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>belonging to a lord</i> or <i>king, royal,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					15.397
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνακτόριον, τό,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνάκτορον</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.65
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξιφίον</span>
			, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.20
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιος, ὁ,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρτεμισία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.113
			</span></i>.</div>
